From e69163a3eb1f7fc27473a625972a4146f2033c46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:00:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(import): refuse STEP records nested past 64
 parentheses before parsing

ruststep's recursive-descent parser overflows the stack on a DATA record
nested about 400 deep (debug, 1 MiB) to 1086 (release, 2 MiB), taking the
process down. A linear byte pre-scan (geometry::import::step_depth) tracks
depth outside strings and comments and refuses past MAX_NESTING = 64,
naming the cap, the entity #id and the line. Called first by
step::parse_with_chord (every model import) and step_csys::read_tool_csys.

Fixes #1075

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
